  "title": "# Build: console-wake-finish (Current profile) - URGENT, front of line ## What Brett said (voice, N…",
  "asked": "# Build: console-wake-finish (Current profile) - URGENT, front of line ## What Brett said (voice, Nov 4 2026) \"Why isn't Follow Amber working?\" -> Follow Amber is on, but his console tab sleeps in the background while he's in the Claude app on a voice call, so console_show commands sit undelivered. Amber offered to bump console wake up the line: \"Yes.\" Book to Ping Paulie (he built console-wake #266) or any free agent. Register id `console-wake-finish` in the `current` profile + banner entry + What Brett said block. ## Do 1. Check what's already live: #288 (merged 12:05 today) carried #266 console-wake (queue commands with TTL/dedupe, deliver on reconnect, wake Chrome via AmberX open_url). Confirm which parts are on main and deployed; close #266 as superseded if fully contained; land #308 (console wake settings help, currently RED) after fixing it. 2. axHub side: branch `claude/amberx-open-url` in MossesX/axHub (amberx device service `open_url`, allowlisted to amberxai.com, high-priority notification fallback) - merge it and redeploy axHub so `amberx.open_url` works. 3. AmberX side: make sure the AmberX app handles open_url (foreground the console tab / open console.amberxai.com in Chrome, or full-screen notification on Android 14+). If a new APK is required, build it and put it where Brett installs from, and tell him in the report and a banner: 'Install the new AmberX APK' with the link. 4. Make delivery automatic: when console_show (Follow Amber) finds no foreground console within 4 s, it wakes it via AmberX and delivers when the tab wakes. Test end to end if possible. - Small and focused. Type-check, tests, PRs merge when CI green, redeploy console + axHub. Never leave tsc/vite/playwright running. Report `_claude/builds/reports/console-wake-finish.md` (what Brett must do: install APK y/n). Commits clean and professional. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches (Brett, Nov 3 2026): a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. An UPGRADE (e.g. Opus → Fable) needs Brett's approval: when you reach one, run `node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs request-upgrade <id> <phase>`, ask once, and stop. Never approve a model switch upgrade yourself (no `act approve` on an upgrade), never relaunch on a higher model.",
